# Python Quality Rules

## Syntax Requirements
- Must pass `python -m py_compile`
- No syntax errors allowed

## Documentation
- All functions must have docstrings
- Module should have module-level docstring
- Complex algorithms need inline comments

## Code Style
- Maximum line length: 100 characters
- Maximum function length: 50 lines
- Maximum file length: 500 lines
- Use 4 spaces for indentation

## Naming Conventions
- Variables: snake_case
- Functions: snake_case
- Classes: PascalCase
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
- Private: _leading_underscore

## Best Practices
- No unused imports
- No wildcard imports
- Use type hints where appropriate
- Handle exceptions explicitly
- Use context managers (with statements)
- Avoid global variables

## Scoring
- Missing docstring: -5 points per function
- Line too long: -1 point per line
- File too long: -10 points
- Unused import: -3 points
- Syntax error: -30 points (critical)
